{"id": "19d8ba37", "ts": 1792295737.0352948, "job": "e595e60f", "type": "review.verdict", "actor": "captain", "data": {"verdict": "FAIL", "review": "### Code Review\n\n**1) Does it meet the spec?**\n**No.** The provided code is for a completely different application (\"TaskMaster\" - a task management app) instead of the requested \"EvalCraft\" (AI Output Evaluator). It fails almost every requirement:\n*   **Wrong App:** It manages tasks/todos instead of AI rubrics and evaluations.\n*   **Wrong Format:** It uses React JSX and ES imports (`lucide-react`, `react`) which cannot run \"directly in browser\" without a build step or CDN configuration. The spec required a single HTML file with `<style>` and `<script>` tags.\n*   **Missing Features:** There is no Rubric builder, Output scorer, Practice mode, or History tab as defined in the spec.\n*   **Missing Dark Mode:** No dark mode toggle or logic is implemented.\n\n**2) Bugs found:**\n*   **Incomplete Code:** The file ends abruptly in the middle of a `<form>` element.\n*   **Environment Error:** Attempting to open this code in a browser will result in a syntax error because browsers do not natively support JSX or bare module imports without a bundler or specific `<script type=\"module\">` setup.\n*   **Logic Mismatch:** The `localStorage` key used is `task_master_data` instead of the specified `evalcraft_rubrics` and `evalcraft_history`.\n\n**3) Verdict:**\n**FAIL**"}}
